---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title={"Free Name Change Checklist for the UK | Change My Name UK"}
  description={"Changing your name in the UK? Get a free personalised checklist of every place to update, in the right order, with what each one needs: passport, DVLA, HMRC, banks and more."}
  path={"/"}
  ogTitle={"Free Name Change Checklist for the UK"}
  bodyClass={"home"}
  footerSeals
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<link rel="preload" as="image" href="/img/hero-couple-720.jpg">

<script is:inline type="application/ld+json">
{
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "WebSite",
 "name": "Change My Name UK",
 "url": "https://changemynameuk.com/",
 "inLanguage": "en-GB",
 "publisher": {
  "@type": "Organization",
  "name": "Change My Name UK",
  "url": "https://changemynameuk.com/",
  "founder": {
   "@type": "Person",
   "name": "Avi Arnon",
   "url": "https://changemynameuk.com/about/"
  },
  "email": "hello@changemynameuk.com"
 }
}
</script>
</Fragment>
<main id="main">
  <section class="hero2">
    <div class="wrap hero2-grid">
      <div class="hero2-copy">
        <p class="trust-badge"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l7 3v5c0 5-3.5 8-7 10-3.5-2-7-5-7-10V6z"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/></svg><span><b>Free, secure and UK-based</b></span></p>
        <h1>Your name, sorted. Every place to tell, in the right order.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Answer a few quick questions and get a free checklist made for you: passport, driving licence, HMRC, banks, employer, pension and the rest, with what each one needs and which to do first.</p>
        <p class="hero-actions"><a class="button big" href="/check/">Start free checklist</a> <a class="button big ghost" href="/check/">Change name after marriage</a> <a class="button big ghost" href="/check/?reason=divorce">Revert name after divorce</a></p>
        <ul class="reassure">
          <li><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5"/></svg>Free, no sign-up</li>
          <li><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5"/></svg>About 3 minutes</li>
          <li><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5"/></svg>Answers stay on your device</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <figure class="hero2-photo">
        <img src="/img/hero-couple-720.jpg" srcset="/img/hero-couple-720.jpg 720w, /img/hero-couple.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 92vw, 440px" alt="Avi and partner smiling in an open-top car on a sunny day" width="720" height="960">
        <figcaption class="hand-note">We're changing ours too. Avi</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="paths" id="paths" aria-labelledby="paths-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Choose your path</p>
      <h2 id="paths-h">Which of these sounds like you?</h2>
      <div class="path-grid">
        <a class="path-card path-wed" href="/check/">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20s-7-4.5-7-10a4 4 0 0 1 7-2.6A4 4 0 0 1 19 10c0 5.5-7 10-7 10z"/></svg>
          <span class="path-tag">Newlyweds and brides-to-be</span>
          <h3>Congratulations. Let's make it official.</h3>
          <p>Planning ahead or already married, your list puts the passport and honeymoon timing first, then everything else, so no ticket or booking name clashes.</p>
          <span class="go">Get my married-name checklist</span>
        </a>
        <a class="path-card path-div" href="/going-back-to-your-name/">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12a8 8 0 0 1 14-5.3M20 4v4h-4M20 12a8 8 0 0 1-14 5.3M4 20v-4h4"/></svg>
          <span class="path-tag">After divorce, going back to your name</span>
          <h3>Your own name, back. Quietly and in the right order.</h3>
          <p>No fuss and no judgement. We show which proof each organisation wants, so you only have to do it once.</p>
          <span class="go">See how going back works</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="how" id="how">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h2>Three steps, about three minutes</h2>
      <ol class="how-steps">
        <li><span class="num">1</span><b>Answer a few questions</b><p>Why you're changing your name, where you live, what documents you have and which accounts you hold.</p></li>
        <li><span class="num">2</span><b>Get your checklist</b><p>Every place to update, grouped into simple steps in the right order, with links to the official forms.</p></li>
        <li><span class="num">3</span><b>Update DVLA, HMRC and your banks</b><p>Work down the list, ticking things off. Your progress is saved on your device. Print it, save it as a PDF or keep a link.</p></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="center"><a class="button big" href="/check/">Start my free checklist</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="inst-bar" aria-label="Organisations your checklist covers">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="inst-h">Your checklist covers the organisations that matter</p>
      <ul class="inst-list">
        <li>HM Passport Office</li>
        <li>DVLA</li>
        <li>HMRC</li>
        <li>HM Land Registry</li>
        <li>Banks and building societies</li>
        <li>Employers and pensions</li>
        <li>NHS and your GP</li>
        <li>Energy, water and council tax</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="inst-note">Built on official GOV.UK guidance, with links to the official forms. Change My Name UK is independent and not part of any of these organisations.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Reviews: add a .reviews section here once there are real, consented reviews.
       Markup: <section class="reviews"><div class="wrap"><h2>...</h2><div class="review-grid">
       <figure class="review"><blockquote>Quote</blockquote><figcaption><b>Sarah M., Surrey</b><span class="verified">Verified</span></figcaption></figure>
       ...</div></div></section> -->
  <section class="story">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="story-card">
        <div class="story-photo"><img src="/img/avi.jpg" alt="Avi Arnon and partner at sunset" width="480" height="480" loading="lazy"></div>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Why I'm building this</p>
          <h2>Hi, I'm Avi</h2>
          <p>I can't wait to marry the love of my life. We're both on our second act, and when we talked about our joint family name, we realised that neither of us had actually finished changing, or re-changing, our previous surnames in all the different places.</p>
          <p>So I set out to build a simple tool that helps people start their joint life in the simplest way possible. I'd love to help you too.</p>
          <p class="signature">Avi</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="more">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">More ways I can help</p>
      <h2>Free help, whatever stage you're at</h2>
      <div class="cols">
        <a class="card tool-card" href="/guides/"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h13v16H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2zM4 21V5"/></svg><h3>Plain-English guides</h3><p>Honeymoon passports, deed polls, double-barrelled names and more.</p><span class="go">Read the guides</span></a>
        <a class="card tool-card" href="/call/"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 12a8 8 0 0 1-11.6 7.1L4 20l1-4.6A8 8 0 1 1 21 12z"/></svg><h3>Talk to me for 15 minutes</h3><p>Tell me how your name change is going and I'll send you a £7 Amazon voucher as thanks.</p><span class="go">Book a call</span></a>
        <a class="card tool-card" href="/beta/"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="M3.5 6l8.5 7 8.5-7"/></svg><h3>Want it done for you?</h3><p>Join a small beta where we find every organisation, prepare the letters and keep track.</p><span class="go">Join the beta</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="guides-strip">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Popular guides</p>
      <div class="cols">
        <a class="card link-card" href="/guides/change-your-name-after-marriage/"><h3>Change your name after marriage</h3><p>The full process, step by step.</p></a>
        <a class="card link-card" href="/guides/honeymoon-passport/"><h3>Honeymoon passport</h3><p>Which name to book your tickets in.</p></a>
        <a class="card link-card" href="/guides/do-i-need-a-deed-poll/"><h3>Do I need a deed poll?</h3><p>Usually not. Here's when you do.</p></a>
      </div>
      <h3 class="more-guides-h">More guides</h3>
      <ul class="more-guides">
        <li><a href="/guides/civil-partnership-name-change/">Change your name after a civil partnership</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/passport-name-change-after-marriage/">Change your passport after marriage</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/driving-licence-name-change/">Change your driving licence and log book</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/double-barrelled-surnames/">Double-barrelled and combined surnames</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/keeping-your-maiden-name/">Keeping your maiden name, or using it at work</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/who-to-tell-checklist/">Who to tell when you change your name</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/married-abroad/">Married abroad: changing your name in the UK</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p><a href="/guides/">All guides</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Common questions</p>
      <h2>The UK rules, in plain English</h2>
      <div class="faq-grid">
        <details><summary>Do I need a Deed Poll after getting married?</summary><p>Not if you're taking your partner's surname or double-barrelling both surnames, because your Marriage Certificate (or civil partnership certificate) is enough. You need one for a new combined surname or a first name change. <a href="/guides/do-i-need-a-deed-poll/">Read more</a>.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What is the difference between a Deed Poll and a Marriage Certificate?</summary><p>A Marriage Certificate is the official record that links your names, so most organisations accept it as proof. A Deed Poll is a document you sign to declare a name change that no certificate covers. Which one you need depends on the name you're moving to.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What do I need to go back to my previous name after divorce?</summary><p>Usually your Final Order (called a Decree Absolute before April 2022) together with your Marriage Certificate, which shows how the names connect. Each organisation sets its own rules, and your checklist shows what each one asks for. <a href="/going-back-to-your-name/">More on going back</a>.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can I use a Deed Poll to go back instead?</summary><p>Yes, some people prefer one, and it's useful if you don't have your divorce papers to hand. An unenrolled Deed Poll needs two witnesses aged 18 or over. <a href="/guides/deed-poll-after-divorce/">Read the guide</a>.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Does it cost anything to change my name?</summary><p>Changing your name is free with almost every organisation. The main cost is a new passport (£102 online or £115.50 by post), paid directly to HM Passport Office. Our checklist is free too.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is the checklist only for marriage?</summary><p>No. It also covers going back to a previous name after a divorce, and changing your name for any other reason.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Who's behind this?</summary><p>Me, Avi Arnon. I'm getting married and going through the same name change maze, so I'm building the tool I wish we had. <a href="/about/">More about me</a>.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Ready to get it sorted?</h2>
      <p>Your personal checklist takes about three minutes. Free, with no sign-up.</p>
      <p><a class="button light big" href="/check/">Get your free checklist</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
</Base>
